# Generated guest.cpp digests, captured before the IR refactor began.
# The IR work must not change the C++ backend's output; this is what proves it.
#
# Columns: fixture  input-sha256  generated-sha256  generated-bytes
# packed.exe was rebuilt to add a memory-source PSHUFB regression fixture.
# memory.exe changed when user-mode CLI/STI lifting became explicit no-ops; the
# generated guest is intentionally refreshed for that lifter behavior change.
#
# The INPUT digest is pinned as well as the output. Without it a rebuilt fixture
# reports as a changed compiler -- a misdiagnosis in the one test whose whole job
# is to tell those apart, and it happened: the fixtures were rebuilt 25 minutes
# after this baseline was first captured and all 22 entries failed as though the
# lifter had changed.
#
# Generated output changed when issue #67 added per-function provenance headers: every
# function now records its source classification, evidence and byte/instruction counts,
# and the file header records the census. Fixture digests are unchanged.

